  "prompt": "Refactor: Change error messages for unsupported commands and known eos error\nhttps://github.com/aristanetworks/anta/blob/main/anta/device.py#L505\n\nThis should be copied to AntaTest handling to get the test context + add back a warning with device context\n\nInterface the change must provide:\nMethod: AsyncEOSDevice._handle_eapi_command_error(self, command: AntaCommand, e: asynceapi.EapiCommandError) -> None\nLocation: anta/device.py\nInputs: \n- **command** \u2013 an\u202fAntaCommand instance representing the eAPI command that was issued (contains attributes such as `command`, `requires_privileges`, `supported`, `returned_known_eos_error`, and mutable `errors` list).  \n- **e** \u2013 an\u202fasynceapi.EapiCommandError exception object with attributes `errors` (list of error strings, may be empty or contain empty strings) and `errmsg` (full error message string).\nOutputs: None (the method mutates `command.errors` and emits log messages). It sets `command.errors` to a cleaned list of error messages \u2013 using the non\u2011empty entries from `e.errors` or, if those are all empty, extracting the relevant part of `e.errmsg`. It also logs an error, warning, or debug message that includes the device name and command context.\nDescription: Processes an EapiCommandError by removing empty error strings, falling back to the parsed `errmsg` when necessary, updating the AntaCommand's error list, and producing a device\u2011specific log entry that reflects privilege issues, unsupported commands, known EOS errors, or generic failures. This method replaces the older `_log_eapi_command_error` and is invoked during async command collection, directly influencing the assertions in the updated tests.",
